<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29487" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">molluscus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		mollis. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Soft</i>: mollusca nux; and <i>absol.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mollu-sca</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>a kind of soft
				nut with a thin shell</i>, Plaut. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 2, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 15,
				22, 24, § 90</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">molluscum</span></b> , i, n., <i>a fungus that grows on the maple-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				16, 27, § 68</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
